course: dictionary
lesson: 8049
title: The word regularly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Regularly means often and at the same times, again and again. When something happens regularly, it keeps coming back on a steady pattern, like every day or every week. «Brush your teeth regularly» means do it again and again, not just once.
explain: Regularly can also mean evenly spaced, with the same distance or time between things. Think of dots placed at equal gaps along a ruler. Ask yourself: is something happening again and again, or are things spaced out equally? Either way, the clue is the steady pattern.
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. «Small amounts put regularly into a money box add up over time» means you put money in again and again, not just once. «Their eclipses happen so regularly that people used them as a clock in the sky» means they come back at predictable times. Swap in often and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Regularly means often and at the same times, again and again.
fact: Regularly can also mean evenly spaced, with the same distance or time between things.
fact: Regularly is an adverb: it tells you how often or how something is done.
fact: «Nurses check temperature, pulse and breathing regularly, even at night.» They check again and again, on a steady pattern.
fact: «A subscription is paying regularly, often every month, for something like music, videos or a game.»
exercise: What does regularly mean in «Brush your teeth regularly»? | * Often, at the same times, again and again | Only if you are sleepy | Very loudly and with lots of noise | Just once, very quickly
exercise: Maths: «The points are regularly spaced along the line.» What does regularly suggest? | Scattered at random, with no pattern | * Evenly spaced, with equal gaps between them | Coloured in different shades | Joined together in a circle
exercise: Which sentence shows something happening at steady times? | «The dog barked once at the door.» | «The shop closed early today.» | «The river froze in winter.» | * «A subscription is paid regularly, often every month.»
test: «Nurses check breathing regularly, even at night.» Why is regularly used here? | To show they forget to check | * To show they check at steady times, again and again | To show they check just once | To show they only check in the morning
test: Which phrase has the same meaning as regularly? | Without any pattern | Once in a blue moon | * Again and again at set times | Never at all
exam: In «Their eclipses happen so regularly that people used them as a clock in the sky», what does regularly tell us? | They are very bright and easy to see | * They come back at predictable, steady times | Their pattern is random, with no order | They are hidden behind clouds most nights
